# Wlan.kext: the net80211 family (E21 D11), FreeBSD's 802.11 stack. The wlan
# core and every plug-in (WEP, TKIP, CCMP, GCMP, AMRR, RSSadapt, xauth, ACL) are
# one module here, the way GENERIC links them into one kernel image: net80211
# never loads a plug-in on demand (ieee80211_load_module() is a stub in
# releng/15.1), so a Wi-Fi driver must find them all present. Every Wi-Fi kext
# depends on this one. Built from this directory's Makefile, not sys/modules.
KEXT_NAME=Wlan
KEXT_ID=org.nextbsd.kpi.Wlan
KEXT_ARCHES="amd64 arm64"
KEXT_MODULE=local
KEXT_KO=wlan.ko
KEXT_CATEGORY=hw-support-lib
KEXT_MATCH=none
KEXT_PERSONALITIES=""
KEXT_FIRMWARE=""
KEXT_REQUIRED="Network-Root"
